0..42 Comment "/// An action over a lambda written twice."
43..46 Comment "///"
47..122 Comment "/// One action on a path, over a lambda that closes over a variable, is one"
123..201 Comment "/// path wherever the source writes it. Two definitions whose bodies write the"
202..258 Comment "/// action unfold to it, and a reflexivity relates them."
259..262 Comment "///"
263..339 Comment "/// The action unfolds to a transport whose motive calls the lambda. The two"
340..415 Comment "/// motives hold two thunks of the lambda, each closing its own copy of the"
416..486 Comment "/// body over its own captures. They compare by those bodies up to the"
487..563 Comment "/// variables each reads free, and by the captures those variables name. The"
564..643 Comment "/// two scopes may lay the captures out apart: one may bind more variables than"
644..688 Comment "/// the other, or bind `g` at another place."
689..692 Comment "///"
693..776 Comment "/// - see: #3807 — the code walk pairs two written calls by function and argument"
777..861 Comment "/// - see: #3920 — the checker declined two motives calling a lambda written twice"
862..949 Comment "/// - see: #3976 — the checker declined two such motives over captures laid out apart"
951..980 Comment "/// The action of `F` on `p`."
